  "rai:dataCollection": "Simulated data generated via ASE (nanoparticle construction), analytical Z^gamma forward model, and abTEM multislice. Real experimental data sourced from published Zenodo records: Zr-ZrO2 nanoparticles (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.12742309), MPEA2 high-entropy alloy (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.17310133), Pt Brownian tomography (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.15531575), RESIRE datasets (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.7819857), AlSiYb alloy (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.2578866), PdPt core-shell Zhou group (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.7733503), PdPt core-shell Yang group (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.8245312), NiPt multi-grained catalyst (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.15321070), AuPd icosahedral nanoparticles (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.14677350).",
  "rai:dataCollectionType": "Automated simulation + published experimental measurements",
  "rai:dataSocialImpact": "No direct social impact. Materials science research tool for advancing atomic-scale 3D/4D imaging of nanoparticles. No human subjects, no PII, no dual-use concerns.",
  "rai:dataLimitations": "Real experimental data limited to publicly available Zenodo records. Brownian Pt tier uses synthetic projections from published reconstructions. Simulated data uses simplified Z^gamma forward model that does not capture dynamical scattering.",
  "rai:dataBiases": "The benchmark is biased toward inorganic metal and oxide nanoparticles, HAADF-STEM acquisition, public Zenodo releases, and high-Z materials with strong contrast. Crystalline catalyst and alloy structures are better represented than biological specimens, low-Z soft materials, bright-field TEM, or in-situ experiments with severe drift and contamination.",
  "rai:personalSensitiveInformation": "None. AET-Bench contains simulated nanoparticles, physical-science microscopy data, reconstruction volumes, atomic coordinates, and benchmark metrics. It contains no human subjects, personal identifiers, demographic attributes, health data, or other sensitive personal information.",
  "rai:dataUseCases": "Intended uses include benchmarking atomic electron tomography reconstruction, atom localization, element classification, 4D trajectory tracking, robustness analysis, and reproducibility studies for materials-science imaging. The dataset is not intended for clinical decision-making, human-subject analysis, surveillance, or unsupported claims about microscopy modalities outside the documented HAADF-STEM and simulation settings.",
  "rai:hasSyntheticData": true,
